{"headword":"מַטָּרָה","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"and (<a data-ref=\"Lamentations 3:12\" href=\"/Lamentations.3.12\">La 3:12</a>) <span dir=\"rtl\">מַטָּרָא</span> <strong>n.f. 1. guard, ward, prison. 2. target, mark</strong> (as <em>kept</em> in the eye, <em>watched</em>, cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, נָצַר\" href=\"/BDB,_נָצַר\", dir=\"rtl\">נָצַר</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 23:26\" href=\"/Proverbs.23.26\">Pr 23:26</a>, and σκόπος (<em>watcher, mark</em>) from σκέπτομαι; perhaps Nab. <span dir=\"rtl\">מט[רתא]</span> Lzb<sup>323</sup>);—always abs.:—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>guard, ward, prison</em>, usually <span dir=\"rtl\">חֲצַר הַמּ׳</span> <em>court of guard</em> (v. i. <a data-ref=\"BDB, חָצֵר\" href=\"/BDB,_חָצֵר\", dir=\"rtl\">חָצֵר</a>) <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 32:2\" href=\"/Jeremiah.32.2\">Je 32:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 32:8\" href=\"/Jeremiah.32.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 32:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.32.12\">12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 33:1\" href=\"/Jeremiah.33.1\">33:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 37:21\" href=\"/Jeremiah.37.21\">37:21</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 38:6\" href=\"/Jeremiah.38.6\">38:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 38:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.38.13\">13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 38:28\" href=\"/Jeremiah.38.28\">28</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 39:14\" href=\"/Jeremiah.39.14\">39:14</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 39:15\" href=\"/Jeremiah.39.15\">15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 3:25\" href=\"/Nehemiah.3.25\">Ne 3:25</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁעַר הַמּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:39\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.39\">12:39</a>."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>target, mark</em> <a data-ref=\"Job 16:12\" href=\"/Job.16.12\">Jb 16:12</a> (fig. of <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>’s chastisement), <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּמַּטָּרָא לַחֵץ</span> <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 3:12\" href=\"/Lamentations.3.12\">La 3:12</a> (sim. <em>id.</em>); lit. only <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:20\" href=\"/I_S